Structure
        Animal
       /      \
     Dog      Cat

Step 1 — Parent Class
class Animal 
{
    void eat() 
    {
        System.out.println("Eating");
    }
}

Step 2 — First Child
class Dog extends Animal 
{
    void bark() 
    {
        System.out.println("Barking");
    }
}

Step 3 — Second Child
class Cat extends Animal 
{
    void meow() 
    {
        System.out.println("Meowing");
    }
}

Step 4 — Main Method
public class Main 
{
    public static void main(String[] args) 
   {
        Dog d = new Dog();
        d.eat();
        d.bark();
        Cat c = new Cat();
        c.eat();
        c.meow();
    }
}

Output :
Eating
Barking
Eating
Meowing
